  "headline": {
    "id": "nvidia-interim-ceo-transition-20261116",
    "date": "2026-11-16",
    "title": "NVIDIA names Colette Kress interim CEO after Jensen Huang’s resignation",
    "summary": "NVIDIA’s November 12 filing says the board accepted Jensen Huang’s resignation as president, CEO and director on November 11, effective immediately. CFO Colette Kress became interim CEO and keeps her finance role; Harvey Jones became board chair. The board is searching for a permanent CEO and says it expects operations, customer commitments and the product roadmap to continue without interruption. That is a continuity commitment, not evidence that future shipments or financing arrangements are guaranteed. The announcement keeps the November 17 earnings schedule. For AI infrastructure buyers, the immediate change is leadership and accountability at a central equipment supplier; the disclosed transition does not quantify a change in delivered compute capacity.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "NVIDIA November 12 Form 8-K, effective November 11",
